### Manual end-to-end walkthrough (VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client).
### Credentials must match AUTH_USERNAME / AUTH_PASSWORD and DEMO_DB_READONLY_* in .env.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api/v1

### 1. Get a token (JSON body; HTTP Basic also works)
# @name auth
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "change-me-admin"
}

###
@token = {{auth.response.body.access_token}}

### 2. Extract metadata from the demo database (host = compose service name)
# @name metadata
POST {{baseUrl}}/db/metadata
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "host": "demo-db",
  "port": 5432,
  "database": "llm_discovery_demo",
  "username": "discovery_reader",
  "password": "change-me-demo-reader"
}

###
@metadataId = {{metadata.response.body.metadata_id}}

### 3. List metadata snapshots
GET {{baseUrl}}/metadata?limit=20&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Metadata detail (copy a column_id from here)
GET {{baseUrl}}/metadata/{{metadataId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Classify a column
POST {{baseUrl}}/classify
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "column_id": "<column_id from step 4>",
  "sample_count": 10
}

### 6. Delete the snapshot (the stored connection is kept)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/metadata/{{metadataId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
